From 1e47554dc394cba458732bb5c5278a22e3ac36ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xi Ruoyao <xry111@xry111.site>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:44:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 63/68] add hack for old-world seccomp sandbox

Add back __NR_fstat and __NR_newfstatat so glibc will use fstat and
newfstatat instead of statx for anything other than statx itself, see
commit 551101e8240b ("io: Do not implement fstat with fstatat").  Also
undefine __ASSUME_STATX to allow statx() itself to fall back in case
some (stupid I'd say) software calls statx() but blacklists the statx
syscall.

Note that this issue is not limited to ABI1.0 (i.e. the fstat/fstatat
implementation is orthogonal to ABI1.0/ABI2.0) but if you hit this issue
on ABI2.0 you should collaborate with the upstreams to figure out an
elegant solution (based on the nullable path support with AT_EMPTY_PATH
on Linux >= 6.11 for statx) instead of using this hack or more stupid
hack (for example, forcing a lower --enable-kernel-version which is done
by some commercial or so-called "community" distros and makes a
Frankenstein ABI).

Signed-off-by: Xi Ruoyao <xry111@xry111.site>
---
 .../sysv/linux/loongarch/fixup-asm-unistd.h   | 21 -------------------
 .../sysv/linux/loongarch/lp64/arch-syscall.h  |  2 ++
 .../linux/loongarch/lp64/kernel-features.h    |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/loongarch/fixup-asm-unistd.h
 create mode 100644 sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/loongarch/lp64/kernel-features.h

diff --git a/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/loongarch/fixup-asm-unistd.h b/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/loongarch/fixup-asm-unistd.h
deleted file mode 100644
index a823a26ad2..0000000000
--- a/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/loongarch/fixup-asm-unistd.h
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,21 +0,0 @@
-/* Regularize <asm/unistd.h> definitions.  LoongArch version.
